{title: In the Sweet By and By}
{artist: Sanford F. Bennett / Joseph P. Webster}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There's a [G]land that is [C]fairer than [G]day
And by [D7]faith we can [G]see it a[D7]far
For the [G]Father waits [C]over the [G]way
To pre[D7]pare us a [G]dwelling place [D7]there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
In the [G]sweet by and [C]by
We shall [G]meet on that [D7]beautiful [G]shore
In the [G]sweet by and [C]by
We shall [G]meet on that [D7]beautiful [G]shore
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We shall [G]sing on that [C]beautiful [G]shore
The me[D7]lodious songs of the [G]blessed
And our [G]spirits shall [C]sorrow no [G]more
Not a [D7]sigh for the [G]blessing of [D7]rest
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
To our [G]bountiful [C]Father a[G]bove
We will [D7]offer our [G]tribute of [D7]praise
For the [G]glorious [C]gift of His [G]love
And the [D7]blessings that [G]hallow our [D7]days
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
